// gather.proto — the shapes a WORKSPACE GATHER is described by: the answer
// of GatherWorkspaces, the read of GetGatherStatus, and the two notices a
// gather sends its caller. AGENT API section.
//
// A GATHER asks many workspaces the same question on one workspace's behalf
// (its CALLER) and brings their answers back as ONE update. Each accepted
// target is prompted as `workspace prompt` would prompt it; its ANSWER is the
// final response of the turn the prompt went into, followed across every move
// the daemon makes of the prompt (held again, joined into a running turn,
// resubmitted, resumed after a restart). Targets never reply on purpose.
//
// THE FIRST UPDATE is one notice, sent at whichever comes first: every
// accepted target resolved (a latch), or the gather's deadline. Each target
// resolved AFTER it is told as its own notice the moment it resolves. A gather
// is durable: its latch and deadline survive a daemon restart and a handover.

